n", 'output': "Evaluation: The current hand (Jack of Spades, Queen of Hearts) has not connected with the flop (4 of Spades, King of Clubs, 3 of Clubs). While you hold overcards to the 3 and 4, the presence of the King on the board is dangerous as it connects well with an opponent's potential calling range. There are no immediate straight or flush draws.\n\nReason: Since the option to Check (0) is available, it is the most prudent play. It allows you to see the Turn card for free without inflating the pot with a weak hand. Folding is unnecessary when checking is free, and betting is risky because you are likely behind any pair or a King.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
